@host = http://localhost:5000

### ---------- REGISTER ----------

### 1. Register a new account -> expect 201
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "yami@pangaea.test",
  "username": "yami",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 2. Same email again -> expect 409
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "yami@pangaea.test",
  "username": "someoneelse",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 3. Same username, different letter case -> expect 409
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "other@pangaea.test",
  "username": "YAMI",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 4. Invalid input (bad email, '@' in username, short password) -> expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "username": "ya@mi",
  "password": "123"
}

### ---------- PROTECTED ----------

### 5. /me WITHOUT token -> expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
